## Why Said exists

A billion and a half people don't speak one language at home — they speak two, woven into the same sentence. They write code in English and yell at the build in Hindi. They send Slack messages that start in English, switch to *"yaar"*, end in *"karna hai"*. It's how India actually talks.

Every voice-dictation tool ever built ignores this. They make you pick a language and live with the consequences.

**Said is built for the way you already speak.**

Hold Caps Lock anywhere on your Mac. Talk however the words come — English, Hindi, or both in the same breath. Let go. Clean, polished text appears under your cursor in any app, in any editor, on any website. It learns from your edits. It runs on your own keys. It costs nothing. The whole thing is in this repo.

