## Highlights

- **Hinglish-native** — code-switches mid-sentence without breaking
- **Sub-second latency** — Caps Lock up, text in. Streaming Rust pipeline, no JS in the hot path
- **Learns from your edits** — fix *"Anish"* to *"Aneesh"* once and Said remembers forever
- **Auto-polish** — drops the *"umm"*s, fixes grammar, formats lists. Sounds like you on a good day
- **Private by default** — no Said server, no telemetry, no analytics. Your audio goes only where your keys say
- **Works everywhere** — Slack, Cursor, browser, terminal, Notion, anywhere a cursor blinks
- **Free forever** — bring your own Local speech and ChatGPT keys (both have generous free tiers)
- **Open source, every line** — fork it, audit it, ship it under MIT

---

## Install

One line on macOS (Apple Silicon or Intel):

```bash
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EMIAC-org/Said/main/install.sh | bash
```

The installer drops a `vp` CLI, a menu-bar status indicator, and a LaunchAgent so Said is ready every time you log in. Three one-time steps:

```bash
vp local_speech-key      # save your Local speech API key
vp auth              # connect ChatGPT for the polish step
vp permissions       # grant macOS Input Monitoring + Accessibility
vp                   # start
```

Then **hold Caps Lock anywhere on your Mac, speak, release.** That's the whole product.

