## Contributing

Said is open source because dictation should be infrastructure, not a SaaS. PRs welcome — especially:

- New STT provider adapters (Whisper, AssemblyAI, ElevenLabs, …)
- Indic-language polish prompts
- Linux & Windows ports
- Domain-specific learning packs (legal, medical, code)

```bash
./dev.sh   # builds the Rust backend, then launches the Tauri dashboard
```

The learning loop is in [crates/voice-polish/src/learning.rs](crates/voice-polish/src/learning.rs). The hotkey path is in [crates/hotkey/src/lib.rs](crates/hotkey/src/lib.rs). Open an issue before a large PR so we can align.

